@startuml
' Sequence of GET /products/{id} in app/main.py: ETag, Cache-Control and 304.
' Render with:  plantuml -tsvg etag-sequence.puml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF8E1
skinparam noteBorderColor #C9A227
skinparam sequenceGroupBackgroundColor #EDF2F7
title GET /products/1 with ETag and Cache-Control

participant "Client\n(browser or proxy cache)" as C
participant "API\nGET /products/{id}" as S

== 1. First request: nothing is cached ==
C -> S : GET /products/1
S -> S : etag = hash of the JSON body\n(here "e1")
S --> C : 200 OK\nETag: "e1"\nCache-Control: public, max-age=60\n{ "name": "API Design handbook", "price": "34.50", ... }
note over C : stores the copy and its ETag.\nThe copy is fresh for 60 s.

== 2. Within 60 seconds: the copy is fresh ==
C -> C : reuses the stored copy
note over C, S : No request is sent: the server does not see it.

== 3. After 60 seconds: the copy is stale, the product has not changed ==
C -> S : GET /products/1\nIf-None-Match: "e1"
S -> S : etag = "e1" again (same body)\nit matches If-None-Match
S --> C : 304 Not Modified\nETag: "e1"\nCache-Control: public, max-age=60\n(no body)
note over C : keeps its copy, now fresh for another 60 s.

== 4. Someone changes the product ==
C -> S : PUT /products/1/price\n{ "price": "39.00" }
S --> C : 200 OK
note over S : the next body gives\nanother ETag, "e2"

== 5. Next revalidation: the old copy is out of date ==
C -> S : GET /products/1\nIf-None-Match: "e1"
S -> S : etag = "e2"\nit does not match "e1"
S --> C : 200 OK\nETag: "e2"\nCache-Control: public, max-age=60\n{ ..., "price": "39.00", ... }
note over C : replaces its copy with the new one.
@enduml
